    "title": "George and Amal Clooney Granted French Citizenship",
    "text": "• George Clooney and his wife Amal Clooney were granted French citizenship.\n• The French government stated the Clooneys contribute to France's international influence and cultural outreach.\n• The naturalizations were announced in the Journal Officiel.\n• A junior minister expressed concerns about potential perceptions of special treatment.\n• Former U.S. President Trump criticized the move.\n• The Clooneys purchased a French estate in 2021 and consider it their primary residence.\n• Amal Clooney was born in Lebanon, raised in the U.K., and naturalized under her maiden name.\n• The twins were born in London.\n• The Foreign Ministry cited a law allowing naturalization for those contributing to France's international influence and economic well-being.\n• The Interior Minister defended the decision.\n• Clooney is learning French.\n• The Clooneys live part-time in a villa in southern France.\n• Clooney has expressed concerns about raising his children in the Hollywood culture.",
